DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261030T130000
DTSTAMP:20261029T145939Z
UID:73eedde50bd43f7a0deea774a4f0cba1@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nCome face-to-face with 
 some different species of spiders from our collections. We will take a loo
 k at spider silk using a Scanning Electron Microscope (SEM) to get a bug's
 -eye view of what it's like to get caught in a spider's web. Scientists\, 
 researchers\, and collections managers are behind the scenes every day\, u
 ncovering new information and taking care of our collection. During Meet a
  Scientist\, you can find them in the Grainger Science Hub . They'll disc
 uss their work and share real items from the museum’s collection of near
 ly 40 million objects. From collections care to field work\, and dinosaurs
  to ecology\, there’s a world of science to explore. Visit the Science H
 ub on select weekdays for an up-close look at what our researchers do ever
 y day.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scien
 tist/meet-a-scientist-spooky-spider-webs
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/meet-a-scienti
 st-spooky-spider-webs
