BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ka-thunk! We Can Prevent Bird Collisions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261106T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261106T130000
DTSTAMP:20261029T145939Z
UID:88f7dc99338e6c961106892aab18af54@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nBirds are vulnerable to colli
 sions caused by light attraction and reflections in windows. Come learn ho
 w you can take concrete action to reduce the risk by being thoughtful abou
 t lighting and treating windows\, both at home and at the office. Visitors
  will meet Adrian Gall\, President and Director of Research at ABR\, Inc.
 \, and Bryan Lenz\, Glass Collisions Program Director at the American Bird
  Conservancy\, to learn how they study bird movements\, especially at nigh
 t\, to better understand the risk of collision. We will also discuss worki
 ng with communities to reduce risks to birds by adjusting lighting\, treat
 ing glass\, and rescuing birds that are downed by collisions or light attr
 action.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scie
 ntist/ka-thunk-we-can-prevent-bird-collisions
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/ka-thunk-we-ca
 n-prevent-bird-collisions
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Ka-thunk! We Can Prevent Bird Collisions
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
