UID:9268ea1881e9601e06f8c889ee79adce@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nJoin us for a performan
 ce in celebration of Native American Heritage Month with the Black Hawk Pe
 rformance Company. The Black Hawk Performance Company seeks to honor the g
 round we dance on\, Mother Earth and the many tribes who have made Illinoi
 s their home. Many tribes like the Ojibwe\, Odawa and Potawatomi and numer
 ous others  have been here for thousands of years and are still here now.
  Most American Indian people\, 70%\, live in urban areas like Chicago now.
  The most famous American Indian leader of historic times was the great Sa
 uk Chief Black Hawk. His name comes from the great black hawks that we see
  all over the state. We honor both his name and our brother the hawk when 
 we say these words. The Black Hawk Performance Company is a sponsored by t
 he American Indian Association of Illinois.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fi
 eldmuseum.org/our-events/cultural-programming/black-hawk-performance-compa
 ny
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/cultural-programming/black-hawk
 -performance-company
